schema: signal
object:
  title: impact-certificates-hypercerts.md's "Built on the AT Protocol" claim looks like a factual error
  type: signal
  signal_type: content
  affected_layer: layer-2-encyclopedia
  interpretation: >-
    The article states hypercerts are "Built on the AT Protocol,
    decentralized, community-owned" directly after stating "Hypercerts are
    NFTs (ERC-1155 standard)... Live on Ethereum, permanent, immutable." AT
    Protocol is the protocol behind Bluesky/the social web, not an Ethereum
    smart-contract standard — this looks like a source-article error or
    hallucination rather than a fact worth propagating as-is. Flagging for a
    human fact-check rather than asserting it as a hypercert claim-evidence
    object.
  proposed_intervention: flag
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/impact-certificates-hypercerts.md
    transformation: synthesized
    authorship: ai-assisted
